Anthony was a human man who lived alone on the second floor of an apartment building in the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Gullet/index|Gullet]] for more than a year. His neighbours knew little of him. He spoke to no one as a rule, went out in a black raiment with a hood, and kept his skin wrapped in bandages. Rings were drawn all over the skin underneath. He was short, about five and a half feet, and was seen coming home with books and strange things and never with anyone else.

He found [[Org/Guren and Guren/People/Amos Guren|Amos Guren]] on the street a few blocks from his office about a week before he died and sold him a [[Phenomena/Feyrock|Feyrock]] necklace, a green stone set in a gold chain, for twenty thousand gold pieces, far under what the stone was worth.

He was found dead in his own apartment, his body held in the air above a ritual circle drawn in red ink, and the lower half of one leg turned to Feyrock. The stone was still creeping upward an inch or two a day, and a piece had been cut from it. No wound or sign of a struggle was found, and his neighbours had heard nothing.
